Since service workers have readonly access to `navigator.location`, use [WindowClient.navigate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WindowClient/navigate) for navigation.

## Navigate on Activation

```javascript
self.addEventListener('activate', event => {
  event.waitUntil(
    self.clients.claim()
      .then(() => self.clients.matchAll({ type: 'window' }))
      .then(clients => {
        return clients.map(client => {
          if ('navigate' in client) {
            return client.navigate('meow.html');
          }
        });
      })
  );
});
```

The `navigate()` method returns a Promise that resolves to the existing WindowClient.

Happy navigating! 🧭

Arrays with the help of ES6 now have uber cool methods! Let's look at them with examples.

