The [webpack module federation](/blog/webpack-module-federation) post resulted in many folks asking me if remote URLs need to be known at build-time? Or is there a way to specify the remotes after building, as runtime configuration somewhere.

Well, we have an easy way to load the component dynamically, here is a suggested method from the docs:

```javascript
function loadComponent(scope, module) {
  return async () => {
    // Initializes the shared scope. Fills it with known provided modules
    // from this build and all remotes
    await __webpack_init_sharing__("default");

    const container = window[scope]; // or get the container somewhere else

    // Initialize the container, it may provide shared modules
    await container.init(__webpack_share_scopes__.default);

    const factory = await window[scope].get(module);
    const Module = factory();

    return Module;
  };
}

